    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d245">

                <pb facs="0755" n="718" sameAs="frus:frus1977-80v16/pg718"/>

                <head>245. Presidential Determination<anchor n="1" xml:id="d245-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <idno type="document-identifier">No. 80–6</idno>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1979-11-14">November 14, 1979</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">MEMORANDUM FOR THE SECRETARY OF STATE</p>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Maintenance of Sanctions Against Zimbabwe-Rhodesia Under Section 408 (b)
                        of the Department of State Authorization Act, Fiscal Years 1980 and
                        1981</item>
                </list>
                <p>Pursuant to Section 408 (b) of the Department of State Authorization Act, Fiscal
                    Years 1980 and 1981 (93 Stat. 405), I hereby determine that it is in the
                    national interest of the United States to continue sanctions against
                    Zimbabwe-Rhodesia at this time.</p>
                <p>You are requested, on my behalf, to report this determination promptly to the
                    Speaker of the House of Representatives and the Chairman of the Committee on
                    Foreign Relations of the Senate.</p>
                <p>You are further requested to report to me immediately upon the conclusion of the
                    present Constitutional Conference on Zimbabwe-Rhodesia being held in London,
                    describing the conclusions of that conference and your recommendations for
                    action by the United States with respect to the termination of sanctions.<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d245-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>This determination shall be published in the <hi rendition="#italic">Federal
                        Register</hi>.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Jimmy Carter</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
